From 3baa8a84ed6fdd481b70da1b218302000dbc8000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew <matthewhale@live.com.au>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:57:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 33/59] XvT targeting keys (U, I, A, R), overcharged shields at
 launch

- R (nearest enemy fighter) also picks shuttles, transports and tugs, as in
  XvT (starfighter, transport and utility genus).
- U: newest craft (one per flight group), from OpenXvT FLIGHT_KEY_U.
- I: nearest warhead homing on the player, else on a friendly craft.
  Targeting the announced warhead clears its space-bar prompt.
- A: nearest craft attacking the current target (aiTargetRef, hostile to
  a craft target), from Player_FindAttackerOfTarget.
- X-Wing's own I (target identification) and U (crosshair target) move to
  Alt+I and Alt+U.
- game.start_overshield: the player launches with both banks at twice
  nominal. No/half-shield mission starts are unchanged.
